  "body": "Part of #637 (step E2c; design in https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/637#issuecomment-6787218007, section 3). Depends on E2a and E2b.\n\n`CarriedField` gains `simulate(&mut self, ops: &[SimOp]) -> Result<(), StockError>`: the moves are shifted by the residual translation (`from`, `to`, the arc centre - a translation keeps an arc's sense and plane) and subtracted on the baked field through `Stock::simulate`'s own tool construction (`spanning_flank`, batched per brick), so every later cut rides the shipped +Z code: true XY arcs (#413), the closed-form flat floor. The clip (`Clip::Block`, #651) is applied at read-back as today; `column_body` reads the baked field through `column_span` (E2b) on the new lattice.\n\nDone means: `carry_engine_agreement` grows a cut-after-flip fixture - the same block, slot from the top, flipped, slot from the new top (one with an XY arc), both engines agree per column on `empty_at`, top and floor to 1e-6 and on `floor_judged`; a second carry (`then`) after a cut agrees too. No shipped verdict changes. After this, #586 moves the holders (`Held`, `rest/across::sweep`, `PriorPlan`) onto an engine-agnostic carried stock with the column arm as default.\n\nLabels wanted: P2, effort:high, area:sim, enhancement, source:agent.\n",
